# title: Phoenix autocall with memory
# category: Structured notes
# underlyings: 1
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: Semi-annual 5% coupons paid when the stock is above 70%, with missed coupons caught up; redeemed early above 100%; capital at risk below 60% at maturity.
#
# Notional 1000. On each observation: if the stock is at or above its
# initial level, the note is redeemed with the coupon (and any missed ones);
# else if it is at or above 70%, the coupon and missed ones are paid; else
# the coupon is remembered. At maturity, below 60% the capital is repaid
# in proportion to the fall (European knock-in).

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot()
    miss = 0
    alive = 1

2027-07-06  2028-01-04  2028-07-06
    if alive = 1 then
        if spot() >= s0 then
            pays 1000 * (1 + 0.05 * (miss + 1))
            alive = 0
        else
            if spot() >= 0.70 * s0 then
                pays 1000 * 0.05 * (miss + 1)
                miss = 0
            else
                miss = miss + 1
            endIf
        endIf
    endIf

2029-01-04
    if alive = 1 then
        if spot() >= 0.70 * s0 then
            pays 1000 * (1 + 0.05 * (miss + 1))
        else
            if spot() < 0.60 * s0 then
                pays 1000 * spot() / s0
            else
                pays 1000
            endIf
        endIf
    endIf
